A||N||5||MontanaFiero||My '72 GMC --almost scary!!||||9||
Z||000000||MontanaFiero||07-16-2001||12:48 AM||||My 1972 GMC pickup has been down for almost a year now, so I decided to crawl under it and find out what was wrong... The tranny would not go into any gear and I had an extremely loud rattling racket coming from the area of the torque converter, so naturally I assume that must be the problem.. I bought a new converter for $45 and began the process of removing the transmission and trasfer case. Hmmmmm. <B>Only one bolt was holding the tranny in place!!!</B> One ear is broken off of the transmission housing, and when I separated the tranny from the motor, the <B>flywheel fell off!!!</B> The flywheel broke in almost a perfect square around the bolts that hold it to the crank.  This ought to be interesting. I sure hope the torque converter is actually bad, 'cause I'm worried about what may have happened to the pump.<P>This could have been a scary situation!!!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||9
Z||000001||fierospeeder||07-16-2001||04:43 AM||||your lucky you heard that noise and decided to fix it.  Imagine driving and your flywheel explodes, or your trans drops on the road creating a huge speed bump for other cars.<P>Glad you came out okay, and the bolt holding the trans didn't give out on you.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Galen||07-16-2001||09:14 AM||||*riding down the road* whats that? a noise.. mm... *pwap* mmm.. that was a odd noise, seems to be loosing power *honk**honk* I wonder wtf they are honking about behind me.. *looking in rear view mirror to see tranny wobbling itself on the road* .. oh ..<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT> <FONT COLOR="gray">-</FONT> <FONT COLOR="purple">"It may be the opinion of the court, but its still wrong"</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ray19nc/download.html" TARGET=_blank>Download FieroProject.com Chat Client v1.22 Today</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||07-16-2001||01:22 PM||||Naw... It won't fall out.<P>I did a 'neutral drop' going about 15 once in my 71 Chevy 2WD truck way back in my younger (and dumber) days. Tranny broke in half right around where the body meets the bellhousing. Front drive shaft twisted in two about half way down. The tranny was upside-down on the crossmember.<P>The back half of the drive shaft made a HE!! of a racket beating up against the underside of the truck til I coasted to a stop... and tranny fluid EVERYWHERE!!! I was REALLY lucky though... Those trucks have the gas tank inside the cab, behind the seat. The driveshaft yanked the rubber gas lines right off when it broke. Lucky for me it also pinched the steel lines up against the bottom of the cab and sealed the lines off. According to the people I was TRYING to show off for, just one little fireball underneath which somehow kept from igniting the hot tranny fluid...<P>Well I was trying to give my friends a show... That wasn't exactly what I had in mind though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||10
Z||000004||Raydar||07-16-2001||03:14 PM||||Knew a guy in H.S. who had a 73 340 Duster. Did a neutral drop one afternoon, and sprayed pieces of a Torqueflite 727 (supposedly bulletproof Mopar tranny) all over the parking lot.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||AusFiero||07-17-2001||09:29 PM||||Know a guy who had an auto once and one of his idiot drunk mates in the passenger seat decided to chuck it into reverse at 80 mph. Needless to say bits of it cut the floorpan to bits and embedded in idiots leg. Poetic justice I thought.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
